n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"left\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [17592186215622 :answer/value "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"left\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-4$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [17592186215623 :answer/value "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"left\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [17592186215624 :answer/value "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"left\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [17592186215625 :answer/value "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"left\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [17592186215626 :answer/value "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"left\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-3$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [17592186216763 :question/worked-solution "To find the mean of a dataset from a histogram, we first convert it into a frequency table.\n\nOn a histogram, the horizontal axis shows the values in the dataset, and the vertical axis tells us how many times each value appears in the dataset.\n\nIn our case, placing the data from the given histogram in a frequency table, we obtain the following.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Time (ms)</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Trials</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$210$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$220$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$230$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$240$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nTo calculate the mean of a dataset from a frequency table, we multiply each value by its frequency, add the results, and divide by the total frequency.\n\nSo, we now extend the table to include a third column for the product of the values and their corresponding frequencies:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Time (ms) ($x$)</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Trials ($f_x$)</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x \\cdot f_x$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$210$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"right\">$210 \\cdot 1 = 210\\phantom{1}\\quad\\quad$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$220$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"right\">$220 \\cdot 4 = 880\\phantom{1}\\quad\\quad$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$230$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"right\">$230 \\cdot 5 = 1150\\quad\\quad$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$240$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"right\">$240 \\cdot 2 = 480\\phantom{1}\\quad\\quad$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nTherefore, the mean reaction time, in milliseconds, is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nMean &= \\frac{210 + 880 + 1150 + 480}{1 + 4 + 5 + 2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2720}{12} \\\\\n&\\approx 227\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186216767 :question/problem "The table shows the daily study times, rounded to the nearest minute, for a group of $50$ students.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Time (min)</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Number of Students</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$30$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$40$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$50$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$60$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$70$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$9$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$80$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nA new time of $120$ minutes is added to the dataset, making $51$ times in total. Which measure (mean or median) remains the same?"] [17592186216767 :question/worked-solution "When a new data point is added, the mean of the dataset *will* change (unless the new data point equals the mean), and the median of the dataset *may* change. In general:\n\n- The mean of the dataset moves toward that new data point.\n- The median of the dataset moves toward that new data point or stays the same.\n\nSince the original mean lies somewhere in the range of values between $30$ and $80$, and the new data point $120$ lies above this range, the mean of the new dataset must be **greater** than the original mean.\n\nNow, to compare the medians, we first calculate the cumulative frequencies.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Time (min)</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Number of Students</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Cumulative Frequency</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$30$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$40$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$13$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$50$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$23$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$60$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$35$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$70$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$9$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$44$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$80$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$50$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nIn the original dataset of $50$ students, the middle lies between the $25$th and $26$th values. From the cumulative frequencies, both of these values correspond to a time of $60$ minutes. Thus, the median is $60$ minutes.\n\nWhen the $120$ is added, the dataset size becomes $51$, so the median is simply the $26$th value. The $26$th value still corresponds to a time of $60$ minutes. Thus, the median remains $60$ minutes.\n\nTherefore, the median remains the same."] [17592186216794 :question/problem "A sign maker creates square aluminum signs. The price $P$, in dollars, of a sign is a linear function of the side length $s$, in inches, as shown in the table below.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Side length, $s$ (inches)</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Price, $P$ (dollars)</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$18.00$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$30.00$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$9$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$42.00$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nFind the relationship between $s$ and $P$."] [17592186216795 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-6$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe table shows three values of $x$ and their corresponding values of $y$. There is a linear relationship between $x$ and $y$. Find the equation representing this relationship."] [17592186216796 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\"><th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th><th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$24$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$33$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$42$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$51$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe table above shows some pairs of $x$ values and $y$ values. Find the linear equation representing the relationship between $x$ and $y$."] [17592186216797 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$3$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$5$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$7$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$9$</th></tr><tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$f(x)$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-7$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-11$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe table shows four values of $x$ and their corresponding values of $f(x)$. There is a linear relationship between $x$ and $f(x)$ that is defined by the equation $f(x) = mx + 7$, where $m$ is a constant. What is the value of $m$?"] [17592186216798 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$s$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$s + 14$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$s + 28$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe table shows three values of $x$ and their corresponding values of $y$, where $s$ is a constant, for the linear relationship between $x$ and $y$. What is the slope of the line that represents this relationship in the $xy$-plane?"] [17592186216799 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$18$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$24$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nFor line $m$, the table shows three $x$-values and their corresponding $y$-values. Line $n$ is the result of translating line $m$ up $2$ units in the $xy$-plane. What is the $x$-intercept of line $n$?"] [17592186216800 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-15$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe table shows two values of $x$ and their corresponding values of $y$. In the $xy$-plane, the graph of the linear equation representing this relationship passes through the point $\\left(\\dfrac{1}{3}, a\\right)$. What is the value of $a$?"] [17592186216801 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$f(x)$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$7$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$11$</td>\n</tr></tbody></table></div>\n\n\nFor the linear function $f$, the table shows three values of $x$ and their corresponding values of $f(x)$. Function $f$ is defined by $f(x) = ax + b$, where $a$ and $b$ are constants. What is the value of $a - b$?"] [17592186216802 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-4t$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$t$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$18$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6t$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$28$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe table shows three values of $x$ and their corresponding values of $y$, where $t$ is a constant. There is a linear relationship between $x$ and $y$. What equation represents this relationship?"] [17592186216803 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$k$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$k+3$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$17$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe table shows two points on a line in the $xy$-plane. The $y$-intercept of the line is $(k - 1, b)$, where $k$ and $b$ are constants. What is the value of $b$?"] [17592186216804 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Year</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">CO2 Level (ppm)</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1990$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$355$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2000$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$335$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe table above shows the atmospheric CO2 level in parts per million (ppm) for the years $1990$ and $2000$. If the relationship between CO2 level and year is linear, find the function $C$ modeling the CO2 level $t$ years after $1990$."] [17592186216805 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\"><tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\"><th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Number of Containers</th><th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Total Weight (tons)</th></tr><tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$104$</td></tr><tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$214$</td></tr><tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$324$</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n\n\nA shipping company tracks the linear relationship between the number of containers, $n$, on a truck and the total weight, $w$, in tons. Find the equation representing the linear relationship between $n$ and $w$."] [17592186216806 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$f(x)$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n</tr></tbody></table></div>\n\n\nFor the linear function $f$, the table shows three values of $x$ and their corresponding values of $f(x)$. If $g(x) = f(x) + 2$, which equation defines $g$?"] [17592186216807 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$f(x)$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-4$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nSome values of the linear function $f$ are shown in the table above. What is the value of $f(4)$?"] [17592186216839 :question/worked-solution "To estimate the median from a histogram, we first convert the histogram into a frequency table.\n\nOn a histogram with groups, the horizontal axis shows the value groups, and the vertical axis tells us how many values fall into each group.\n\nIn our case, we build the frequency table below and compute cumulative frequencies.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Value</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Frequency</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Cumulative Frequency</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15-18$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$7$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$7$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$18-21$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$21-24$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$24-27$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$17$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$27-30$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$19$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThus, the total number of values is\n\n$$\n7+5+3+2+2=19\n$$\n\nSince this is an odd number, the median is the value in position\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{19+1}{2}=\\dfrac{20}{2}=10\n$$\n\nNow we determine where the $10$th value falls. Looking at the cumulative frequency column in our table, we see the following:\n\n- Up to the first row, the table covers $7$ positions in total.\n- Up to the second row, the table covers $12$ positions in total.\n\nTherefore, the $10$th value falls in the second interval, which is\n$18 - 21$\nas shown below.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Value</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Frequency</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Cumulative Frequency</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15-18$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$7$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$7$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"Moccasin\">$18-21$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"Moccasin\">$12$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$21-24$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$24-27$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$17$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$27-30$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$19$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of the median is $18$."] [17592186216840 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Value $(x)$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Frequency $(f)$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$22-25$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$25-28$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$7$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$28-31$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$31-34$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$34-37$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe frequency table above shows the number of values in a dataset that fall into each group. Rounded to one decimal place, what is the largest possible value of the mean?"] [17592186216840 :question/worked-solution "To estimate the mean from grouped data, we first use the frequency table.\n\nSince we wish to find the *largest possible value* of the mean, we record $x_{\\textrm{max}}$, the largest possible value of $x$ for each group.\n\nThen, we calculate $f\\cdot x_{\\textrm{max}}$ for each row.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Value $(x)$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Frequency $(f)$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x_{\\textrm{max}}$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$f\\cdot x_{\\textrm{max}}$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$22-25$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$25$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4\\cdot 25 = 100$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$25-28$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$7$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$28$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$7\\cdot 28 = 196$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$28-31$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$31$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2\\cdot 31 = 62$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$31-34$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$34$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5\\cdot 34 = 170$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$34-37$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$37$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3\\cdot 37 = 111$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nTherefore, the largest possible value of the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nlargest possible mean &= \\frac{100 + 196 + 62 + 170 + 111}{4 + 7 + 2 + 5 + 3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{639}{21} \\\\\n&\\approx 30.4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place."] [17592186216859 :question/problem "For the linear relationship $4x + 2y = 12$, complete the table below with the corresponding $y$-values for the given $x$-values.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\"><th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th><th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-2$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [17592186216859 :question/worked-solution "Notice that each table gives function values at $x=-2,0$, and $2$.\n\nTo determine which table is correct, we first express $y$ in terms of $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x + 2y &= 12 \\\\\n2y &= 12 - 4x \\\\\ny &= 6 - 2x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we’ll analyze each of the given values of $x$ in turn.\n\n- For $x = -2{:}$\n$$\n\\displaystyle y|= 6 - 2(-2); = 6 + 4; = 10\n$$\n- For $x = 0{:}$\n$$\n\\displaystyle y|= 6 - 2(0); = 6 - 0; = 6\n$$\n- For $x = 2{:}$\n$$\n\\displaystyle y|= 6 - 2(2); = 6 - 4; = 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the filled-in table is the following:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\"><th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th><th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-2$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [17592186216862 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-2$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-5$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$7$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nSome values of $x$ and the corresponding values of $y$ are shown in the table above. There is a linear relationship between $x$ and $y$. Find this relationship, and express it in standard form."] [17592186216863 :question/problem "For the linear function $f(x) = 7x + 1$, complete the table below with the corresponding $f(x)$ values for the given $x$-values.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\"><th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th><th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$f(x)$</th></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-1$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [17592186216863 :question/worked-solution "To find the missing values in the table, we substitute each $x$ into\n\n$$\nf(x) = 7x + 1\n$$\n\nFor $x = -1{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(-1) &= 7(-1) + 1 \\\\\n&=-7 + 1 \\\\\n&=-6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x = 1{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(1) &= 7(1) + 1 \\\\\n&= 7 + 1 \\\\\n&= 8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x = 2{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(2) &= 7(2) + 1 \\\\\n&= 14 + 1 \\\\\n&= 15\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the filled-in table is the following:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\"><th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th><th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$f(x)$</th></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-1$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-6$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [17592186216864 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$z$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-3b$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2b$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6b$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$31$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe table shows three points on a line in the $yz$-plane and their corresponding values of $z$, where $b$ is a nonzero constant. Which equation represents the line?"] [17592186216865 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$f(x)$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-16$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nSome values of the linear function $f$ are shown in the table above. If $x$ can be any real number, what is the value of $f(12)$?"] [17592186216866 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$f(x)$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$7$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nSome values of the linear function $f$ are shown in the table above. In the $xy$-plane, the line $y=f(x)$ passes through the point where $x=\\dfrac12$. Find the $y$-coordinate of this point."] [17592186216867 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-6$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe table above shows some values of $x$ and their corresponding values of $y$. There is a linear relationship between $x$ and $y$. What is the $x$-intercept of the line represented by this relationship in the $xy$-plane?"] [17592186216868 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\"><tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Length of Rope (m)</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Weight Supported (kg)</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$22$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$33$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$44$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nAn engineer tracks the linear relationship between rope length, $\\ell$, and the weight supported, $w$, in kilograms, of a particular load-balancing machine. Which equation represents the linear relationship between $\\ell$ and $w$? Express your answer in standard form."] [17592186216869 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6k$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-5$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$9k$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-7$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe table shows two points on a line in the $xy$-plane, where $k$ is a nonzero constant. Find the equation that represents the line in terms of $x$ and $y$ only."] [17592186216871 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\"><tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\"><th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th><th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th></tr><tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$11$</td></tr><tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td></tr><tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-5$</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe table above shows three $x$-values and their corresponding $y$-values that lie on the line $u$ in the $xy$-plane. Line $v$ is the result of translating line $u$ up $8$ units in the $xy$-plane. Which of the following equations represents the line $v$?"] [17592186216872 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe table above shows three $x$-values and their corresponding $y$-values that lie on the line $k$ in the $xy$-plane. Line $l$ is the result of translating line $k$ down $2$ units in the $xy$-plane. What is the $x$-intercept of the line $l$?"] [17592186216883 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"><strong>$x$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"><strong>$f(x)$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$19$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$19$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe graph of a quadratic function $y = f(x)$ passes through the points given by their $(x,y)$-coordinates in the table above. Find the expression of the function in terms of $x$."] [17592186216884 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$g(x)$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\dfrac{8}{3}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe table above shows three $x$-values and their corresponding values of $g(x)$, where $g(x)=\\dfrac{f(x)}{x+1}$ and $f$ is a linear function. What is the equation of the function $f(x)$?"] [17592186216884 :question/worked-solution "First, since\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\dfrac{f(x)}{x+1}\n$$\n\nwe can write $f$ in terms of $g$ by multiplying both sides by $(x+1){:}$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{array}{rl}\\displaystyle g ( x ) & \\displaystyle  = {\\displaystyle \\frac{f ( x )}{x + 1}} \\\\ \\displaystyle ( x + 1 ) \\cdot  g ( x ) & \\displaystyle  = ( x + 1 ) \\cdot  {\\displaystyle \\frac{f ( x )}{x + 1}} \\\\ \\displaystyle ( x + 1 ) \\cdot  g ( x ) & \\displaystyle  = \\cancel{( x + 1 )} \\cdot  {\\displaystyle \\frac{f ( x )}{\\cancel{x + 1}}} \\\\ \\displaystyle ( x + 1 ) g ( x ) & \\displaystyle  = f ( x )\\end{array}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=(x+1)g(x)\n$$\n\nSubstituting in each given value of $x$, we find coordinates on the line $y=f(x){:}$\n\n- For $x=2$, we have\n$$\n\\displaystyle f(2)=(2+1)\\cdot g(2)=(3)\\cdot 1=3.\n$$\nSo, the point $(2,3)$ is on the line.\n- For $x=4$, we have\n$$\n\\displaystyle f(4)=(4+1)\\cdot g(4)=(5)\\cdot 2=10.\n$$\nSo, the point $(4,10)$ is on the line.\n- For $x=8$, we have\n$$\n\\displaystyle f(8)=(8+1)\\cdot g(8)=(9)\\cdot \\dfrac{8}{3}=24.\n$$\nSo, the point $(8,24)$ is on the line.\n\nSo, we now have a table of values for $y = f(x)$.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$f(x)$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$24$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nSince $f$ is a linear function, it can be written as\n\n$$\nf(x)=mx+c\n$$\n\nNow, we find the slope $m$ using the points\n\n$$\n(x_1, y_1)=(2,3)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n(x_2, y_2)=(4,10){:}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\frac{y_{2} - y_{1}}{x_{2} - x_{1}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{10 - 3}{4 - 2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{7}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the $y$-intercept $c$ using the point $(2,3){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3 &= \\frac{7}{2}(2) + c \\\\\n3 &= 7 + c \\\\\nc &= -4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function is\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\dfrac{7}{2}x - 4\n$$"] [17592186216906 :question/worked-solution "To estimate the mean from a histogram, we first convert the histogram into a frequency table.\n\nOn a histogram with groups, the horizontal axis shows the value groups, and the vertical axis tells us how many values fall into each group.\n\nIn our case, we build the frequency table below and record $x_{\\textrm{mid}}$, the middle value of $x$ for each group. Then, we calculate $f\\cdot x_{\\textrm{mid}}$ for each row.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Weight $(x)$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Packages $(f)$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x_\\text{mid}$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$f \\cdot x_\\text{mid}$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0-10$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4\\cdot 5=20$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10-20$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6\\cdot 15= 90$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$20-30$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$25$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6\\cdot 25 =150$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$30-40$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$35$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4\\cdot 35= 140$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nTherefore, our estimate of the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nMean &= \\frac{20 + 90 + 150 + 140}{4 + 6 + 6 + 4} \\\\\n&= \\frac{400}{20} \\\\\n&= 20\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186216919 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"><strong>Ivy</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3.6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3.8$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4.0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3.9$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4.2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"><strong>Jack</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4.4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4.2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4.0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3.8$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$x$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nIvy and Jack each attempted the math test five times, and their scores are represented in the table above. The mean score for Jack’s attempts was $0.2$ greater than the mean score for Ivy’s attempts. What is the value of $x$?"] [17592186216973 :question/worked-solution "To calculate the smallest possible range, we take the smallest possible maximum value and subtract the largest possible minimum value.\n\nLet's start by turning our histogram into a frequency table.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Value</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Frequency</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$30-\\bbox[3pt, gainsboro]{35}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$36-37$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$38-40$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$41-43$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$7$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt, gainsboro]{44}-51$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nLooking at the table,\n\n- the smallest possible maximum value is $44$, and\n- the largest possible minimum value is $35$.\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible range is\n\n$$\n44 - 35 = 9\n$$"] [17592186216992 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$d(x)$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-3$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-6$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe table above shows three values of $x$ and their corresponding values of $d(x)$, where $d(x)=\\dfrac{r(x)}{x + 1}$ and $r$ is a linear function. What is the $y$-intercept of the graph of $y=r(x)$ in the $xy$-plane?"] [17592186217343 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$g(x)$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$7$</td></tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$13$</td></tr>\n<tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$19$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nSome values of the linear function $g$ are shown in the table above. Which of the following defines $g$?"] [17592186217344 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$20$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe table shows three values of $x$ and their corresponding values of $y$. There is a linear relationship between $x$ and $y$. Which of the following equations represents this relationship?"] [17592186217349 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$9$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$18$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe table above shows some pairs of $x$ values and $y$ values. Which of the following linear equations represents\nthe relationship between $x$ and $y$?"] [17592186217355 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\"><tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\"><th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Number of Containers</th><th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Total Weight (tons)</th></tr><tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$104$</td></tr><tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$214$</td></tr><tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$324$</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n\n\nA shipping company tracks the linear relationship between the number of containers, $n$, on a truck and the total weight, $w$, in tons. Which equation represents the linear relationship between $n$ and $w$?"] [17592186217356 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$20$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$40$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$60$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nFor line $p$, the table shows three $x$-values and their corresponding $y$-values. Line $q$ is the result of translating line $p$ up $3$ units in the $xy$-plane. What is the $x$-intercept of line $q$?"] [17592186217357 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\"><tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\"><th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Item</th><th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Cost per Item</th></tr><tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">Pen</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\$2.00$</td></tr><tr data-next-row=\"true\"><td data-cell-align=\"center\">Notebook</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\$5.00$</td></tr><tr><td data-cell-align=\"center\">Folder</td><td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\$3.00$</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n\n\nA teacher buys pens, notebooks, and folders for a workshop. If the total cost is $\\$100$ for $x$ pens, $y$ notebooks, and $z$ folders, which of the following expresses $y$ in terms of $x$ and $z$?"]}
